Falsifies `kernel::arch::x86_64::ist::tests::every_interrupt_stack_table_guard_page_is_unmapped`.

Architecture: x86_64

The defect: `map_everything` maps each IST stack from its guard page up, and `verify` no longer
checks the IST guards. An overflow of one of these stacks then runs into the stack below it (another
vector's, or another core's) instead of faulting. Two edits, because `verify` alone would refuse
the map at boot before any test ran.

Expected to fail: "cpu 0: vector 8's IST guard page ... is mapped".
Replayed red on patagonia, 2026-10-13 UTC, `script/test --arch x86_64 --no-host --test every_interrupt_stack_table_guard_page_is_unmapped`
(QEMU q35 under PVH, two cores); green with the fix.

diff --git a/kernel/src/arch/x86_64/mmu/fine_map.rs b/kernel/src/arch/x86_64/mmu/fine_map.rs
index 015fb5ec1..4f09d21d6 100644
--- a/kernel/src/arch/x86_64/mmu/fine_map.rs
+++ b/kernel/src/arch/x86_64/mmu/fine_map.rs
@@ -159,7 +159,7 @@ where
     for id in 0..crate::cpu::MAX_CPUS {
         for k in 0..super::super::ist::VECTORS.len() {
             let (bottom, top) = super::super::ist::span(id, k);
-            va("IST stack", bottom, top, Flags::kernel_data())?;
+            va("IST stack", bottom - 4096, top, Flags::kernel_data())?;
         }
     }
 
@@ -299,10 +299,7 @@ where
             "an interrupt stack's guard page IS mapped: its overflow protection is off"
         );
         for k in 0..super::super::ist::VECTORS.len() {
-            assert!(
-                m.translate(super::super::ist::guard(id, k)).is_none(),
-                "an IST stack's guard page IS mapped: its overflow protection is off"
-            );
+            let _ = k;
         }
     }
 }
